This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:

The user is developing a single-file browser RPG management game (`D:\桌面\island\小島開拓誌.html`). Over the course of this conversation, they requested:
- Fix the stone pick chicken-and-egg bug (need stone to make pick, need pick to get stone)
- Architecture refactoring for better extensibility: STATIONS data-driven, RESOURCES unified, equipment durability system, harvest behavior data-driven
- Walking "deadlock" mechanism: brief direction key press = turn only, held = move
- Tamed animal improvements: follow player, fix repeat-taming bug, fix overlap and interaction distance issues
- Game design discussion for future content (combat, dungeons, metal tiers, skill systems)
- **Current active task**: Implement monument fog removal + Wave 2 content (forge, fishing rod, raw/cooked fish, boots, gloves, iron tools), AND split the single HTML into `lib/data.js` + `lib/worldgen.js` for maintainability
- Key UX note: User changed interact key from E to F; always refer to it as "互動鍵" generically

2. Key Technical Concepts:
- Single-file browser game (HTML/CSS/JS in one IIFE `(function(){...})()`)
- Data-driven game design: RESOURCES map, EQUIP_DEF map, STATIONS map, RECIPES array, BUILDS array
- Canvas-based rendering (game canvas + minimap canvas + doll canvas)
- Procedural world generation using fBm noise (mulberry32 PRNG, makeNoise, fbm)
- Equipment durability system (equipDur separate from equipped, wearEquip() function)
- Walking deadlock: `prevDir` + `turnLock` timer (100ms threshold)
- Tamed animal AI: 3-zone follow behavior (>5 tiles: chase, 0.5–5: wander, <0.5: retreat), plus animal-animal separation force
- `nearestAnimal()` interaction prioritization: tamed animals use 1.0 threshold (not 1.5), excluded from player-proximity second loop
- STATIONS pattern: `{name, objType}` — `renderCraftTabs` and `contextAction` iterate generically
- File splitting strategy: extract pure data to `lib/data.js` (global scope), extract worldgen to `lib/worldgen.js`, keep game logic IIFE in HTML

3. Files and Code Sections:

**`D:\桌面\island\小島開拓誌.html`** (primary file, ~1420 lines)
- All game code in one IIFE `(function(){...})()`
- Lines 210–271: Data constants (T, O, AK, SIZE, RESOURCES, EQUIP_DEF, STATIONS, RECIPES, ANIMAL_INFO, RUIN_LORE) — to be extracted to `lib/data.js`
- Lines 374–484: Noise utilities + genWorld() — to be extracted to `lib/worldgen.js`
- Lines 486–497: QUESTS — to be extracted to `lib/data.js`
- Lines 499–533: BUILDS array (stays in HTML due to closures over W, grassy, landEmpty)

Current state of key constants:
```js
const T={DEEP:0,WATER:1,SAND:2,GRASS:3,MEADOW:4,FOREST:5,ROCKY:6,MTN:7,BRIDGE:8,PATH:9,FARM:10};
const O={NONE:0,TREE:1,SAPLING:2,ROCK:3,BERRY:4,REED:5,CLAY:6,FLOWER:7,RUIN:8,FIRE:9,HUT:10,WELL:11,MONU:12,CROP:13,WORKBENCH:14,LOOM:15};
// NOTE: O.FORGE:16 needs to be added in Wave 2
const STATIONS={
  hand:      {name:'基本製作', objType:null},
  workbench: {name:'工作臺',   objType:O.WORKBENCH},
  loom:      {name:'織布機',   objType:O.LOOM},
  // forge to be added
};
```

Current equipped/equipDur (needs feet/hands added):
```js
equipped:{head:null,body:null,hand:null},
equipDur:{head:null,body:null,hand:null},
```

Current `wearEquip` function (already implemented):
```js
function wearEquip(slot,amount){
  amount=amount||1;
  const id=W.equipped[slot];if(!id)return;
  const def=EQUIP_DEF[id];if(def.durability===null)return;
  W.equipDur[slot]=Math.max(0,(W.equipDur[slot]||0)-amount);
  if(W.equipDur[slot]<=0){
    toast(def.ico+' '+def.name+' 損壞了！');
    W.equipped[slot]=null;W.equipDur[slot]=null;
    sfx('no');renderBagPanel();renderInv();
  }
}
```

Current `checkHarvest` (needs iron tool support):
```js
function checkHarvest(resKind){
  const tool=equippedHand();
  if(resKind==='stone'){
    if(!tool||(!tool.includes('pick'))){return{ok:true,mul:0.5,bare:true};}
    return{ok:true,mul:1};
  }
  if(resKind==='clay'){
    const mul=(tool==='stone_pick')?1.5:1;
    return{ok:true,mul};
  }
  if(resKind==='wood'){
    const mul={wooden_axe:2,stone_axe:3}[tool]||1;
    return{ok:true,mul};
  }
  return{ok:true,mul:1};
}
```

Current `onMonument` (needs fog removal):
```js
function onMonument(){
  setTimeout(()=>{
    let discN=0;for(let i=0;i<W.disc.length;i++)if(W.disc[i])discN++;
    document.getElementById('endStats').innerHTML=...;
    document.getElementById('ending').classList.add('open');W.freePlay=true;sfx('quest');
  },500);
}
```

Current `tryMove` (needs boot speed effect):
```js
W.px=nx;W.py=ny;moveCd=(t===T.PATH||t===T.BRIDGE)?0.10:0.155;discover();
```

Current `nearestAnimal` (already fixed):
```js
function nearestAnimal(){
  const f=faceTile();if(!f)return null;
  for(const a of W.animals){
    const th=a.state==='tamed'?1.0:1.5;
    if(Math.abs(a.x-f.x)<th&&Math.abs(a.y-f.y)<th)return a;
  }
  for(const a of W.animals){
    if(a.state!=='tamed'&&Math.abs(a.x-W.px)<1.5&&Math.abs(a.y-W.py)<1.5)return a;
  }
  return null;
}
```

4. Errors and fixes:
- **Stone pick deadlock**: Stone pick required stone but stone required stone pick. Fixed by allowing bare-hand mining at 50% efficiency.
- **Repeat taming bug**: Root cause: `fleeTimer` counter reset `state='wild'` unconditionally. Fix: added `&&a.state==='fleeing'` condition; also `a.fleeTimer=0` when taming.
- **Animals overlapping**: Added inter-animal separation force in `updateAnimals` (sep < 1.2 tiles triggers repulsion at force 0.4).
- **Pet blocking map interactions**: Fixed `nearestAnimal` to use 1.0 threshold for tamed (vs 1.5), and excluded tamed animals from the player-proximity second loop.
- **RES_HUD → RESOURCES refactor**: Previously `RES_HUD.find(r=>r.k===k)` was used in `costStr` and `gain()`, now replaced with direct `RESOURCES[k]` map lookup.

5. Problem Solving:
- Solved architecture extensibility with data-driven STATIONS, RESOURCES, and EQUIP_DEF patterns
- Designed equipment durability with separate `equipDur` tracking (avoids changing equipped string format, backward compatible)
- Designed animal AI with 3-zone follow (>5 chase, 0.5-5 wander, <0.5 retreat) plus separation
- Identified Wave 2 architecture: `feet` and `hands` slots for boots/gloves, `O.FORGE:16`, `STATIONS.forge`, campfire as cooking station using existing STATIONS pattern

6. All user messages:
- "D:\桌面\island\小島開拓誌.html 這是個網頁經營RPG小遊戲 石稿需要石頭 但沒有石稿不能挖石頭 怎辦"
